  "script": "I managed customer pickups at a small furniture store. A man bought a $1,200 leather chair, loaded it himself, then filed a chargeback claiming he never received it. Our signed receipt helped, but he said the signature was forged. Then our salesperson recognized the chair in his public marketplace listing, photographed in the same garage shown on his ID. The listing even said purchased yesterday, changed my mind. Useful detail. We saved screenshots, the loading-dock video, his vehicle plate, and the message where he offered delivery for extra cash. The bank denied the chargeback within two days. He deleted the listing and called us thieves for keeping his payment. My manager offered to accept a normal return under the posted policy. He refused because someone had already bought the chair. So the chair was missing, except for the buyer, the listing, the sale, and the money. A remarkably crowded disappearance.",
